In-process x86-64 JIT for VU1 blocks (GOW_VU1N_X64, experimental): a block the game reaches without native code is
translated at its first slot setup, in microseconds, without a compiler or files, and registered like the build's blocks.
- ps2_vu1_x64.inl (new): vu1x::translate is a line-by-line port of tools/vu1/vu1n_gen.py gen_block() (structural checks,
  lower/upper order, MAC / clip flag model with flush, tail records and pushes, ld / ldn choice with the entry assumption
  "vf00 only", VI backups for branches, D/T exits); each generated statement becomes a helper call running the same
  vu1n:: code, and the inline tier (default on, GOW_VU1X_INLINE=0 = off) emits SSE for FMAC (MADD/MSUB overflow falls to
  the helper), MOVE, LQ/SQ/LQI/SQI, integer ALU and the I-bit store. System V and Windows x64 conventions, xmm0-5 only,
  tail jump to the next block (VU1NativeAccess::chainFn), RWX code chunks never freed. [vu1x] counters in GOW_VU1N_DIAG.
- ps2_vu1_native.inl: slotFor compiles a missing block before giving up on it; ps2_vu1_native.h: chainFn, jitHash.
- ps2_vu1_jit.inl (patch 17's background compiler): the entries the game missed go to vu1n_gen.py as --heads (blocks that
  start where no static head is: a program right after another, the pc the exact engine hands back);
  GOW_VU1N_JIT_HEADS=all for tests.
- tests: vu1_jit_test x64 (digest must equal the compiled-in blocks); vu1_x64_fuzz_test (random programs: x64,
  x64-calls, module = vu1n_gen.py's code built by clang with every entry as a head, exact).
Checked on Linux (clang 18): vu1_jit_test x64 digest 7c9d4a139489ff09 = compiled-in blocks; fuzz seeds 1-12 (4 images x 6
trials) inline = calls; seeds 1, 4, 5, 7, 11 x64 = module digest, run by run and in native block counts; 20 images x 10
trials soak (4,800 runs, 1.55 M native blocks, 1,323 blocks compiled, ~10-65 us each). Windows: the runtime cross-built
with MinGW-w64 GCC and run under Wine: same 7c9d4a139489ff09, same fuzz digests as Linux for seeds 1 and 4, inline =
calls for seed 7 (seed 7 differs from Linux in the exact engine alone: GCC vs clang build of existing runtime code).
Transform loop (8 vertices): exact engine 17.3 us, x64 JIT 1.27 us (inline) / 1.48 us (calls), build's code 0.82 us.

